IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cp1-nouns`
IMPORT `cp1-amount-helpers`
IMPORT `cp1-div-a-employee-employer-contributions`

-- Tests of cp1-div-a-employee-employer-contributions.l4: sections 8 and 9.
-- Every expected value was worked out by hand from the text of the section (line numbers are in the module) before
-- the file was run. The rates and maximums below are ILLUSTRATIVE figures in the style of 2024 (employee base rate
-- (4.95%), first additional (1%), second additional (4%); maximum pensionable earnings 68,500; additional maximum 73,200;
-- exemption 3,500). They are test inputs, not readings of Schedules 1 and 2 (piece cp6) or of section 18.
-- Dollars are exact: L4 NUMBER is a rational.

§ `Tests -- section 8(1) to (1.2): the employee's three contributions`

-- s 8(1): (4.95%) of the lesser of (wages - exemption) and (maximum contributory earnings - provincial amount)
#ASSERT `s 8(1) — the employee's base contribution for the year` (4.95%) 80_000 3_500 65_000 NOTHING EQUALS 3_217.5
#ASSERT `s 8(1) — the employee's base contribution for the year` (4.95%) 30_000 3_500 65_000 NOTHING EQUALS 1_311.75
#ASSERT `s 8(1) — the employee's base contribution for the year` (4.95%) 68_500 3_500 65_000 NOTHING EQUALS 3_217.5
#ASSERT `s 8(1) — the employee's base contribution for the year` (4.95%) 68_499 3_500 65_000 NOTHING EQUALS 3_217.4505
#ASSERT `s 8(1) — the employee's base contribution for the year` (4.95%) 68_501 3_500 65_000 NOTHING EQUALS 3_217.5
#ASSERT `s 8(1) — the employee's base contribution for the year` (4.95%) 80_000 3_500 65_000 (JUST 10_000) EQUALS 2_722.5
#ASSERT `s 8(1) — the employee's base contribution for the year` (4.95%) 2_000 3_500 65_000 NOTHING EQUALS (0 MINUS 74.25)
#ASSERT `s 8(1) — the employee's base contribution for the year` (4.95%) 3_500 3_500 65_000 NOTHING EQUALS 0

-- s 8(1.1): (1%) of the same lesser amount, for 2019 and each subsequent year
#ASSERT `s 8(1.1) — the employee's first additional contribution for the year` 2024 (1%) 80_000 3_500 65_000 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 650
#ASSERT `s 8(1.1) — the employee's first additional contribution for the year` 2019 (1%) 80_000 3_500 65_000 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 650
#ASSERT `s 8(1.1) — the employee's first additional contribution for the year` 2018 (1%) 80_000 3_500 65_000 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(1.1) — the employee's first additional contribution for the year` 2024 (1%) 30_000 3_500 65_000 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 265
#ASSERT `s 8(1.1) — the employee's first additional contribution for the year` 2024 (1%) 80_000 3_500 65_000 (JUST 5_000) EQUALS JUST 600

-- s 8(1.2): (4%) of the amount by which the wages (not exceeding the additional maximum) exceed the maximum, less any provincial amount, for 2024 on
#ASSERT `s 8(1.2) — the employee's second additional contribution for the year` 2024 (4%) 80_000 73_200 68_500 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 188
#ASSERT `s 8(1.2) — the employee's second additional contribution for the year` 2024 (4%) 70_000 73_200 68_500 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 60
#ASSERT `s 8(1.2) — the employee's second additional contribution for the year` 2024 (4%) 68_500 73_200 68_500 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 8(1.2) — the employee's second additional contribution for the year` 2024 (4%) 60_000 73_200 68_500 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 8(1.2) — the employee's second additional contribution for the year` 2024 (4%) 73_200 73_200 68_500 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 188
#ASSERT `s 8(1.2) — the employee's second additional contribution for the year` 2024 (4%) 90_000 73_200 68_500 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 188
#ASSERT `s 8(1.2) — the employee's second additional contribution for the year` 2024 (4%) 80_000 73_200 68_500 (JUST 1_000) EQUALS JUST 148
#ASSERT `s 8(1.2) — the employee's second additional contribution for the year` 2023 (4%) 80_000 73_200 68_500 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 9(1) to (1.2): the employer's three contributions`
#ASSERT `s 9(1) — the employer's base contribution for the year in respect of an employee` (4.95%) 80_000 3_500 65_000 NOTHING EQUALS 3_217.5
#ASSERT `s 9(1) — the employer's base contribution for the year in respect of an employee` (4.95%) 30_000 3_500 65_000 NOTHING EQUALS 1_311.75
#ASSERT `s 9(1) — the employer's base contribution for the year in respect of an employee` (4.95%) 80_000 3_500 65_000 (JUST 10_000) EQUALS 2_722.5
#ASSERT `s 9(1.1) — the employer's first additional contribution for the year in respect of an employee` 2024 (1%) 80_000 3_500 65_000 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 650
#ASSERT `s 9(1.1) — the employer's first additional contribution for the year in respect of an employee` 2018 (1%) 80_000 3_500 65_000 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9(1.1) — the employer's first additional contribution for the year in respect of an employee` 2019 (1%) 80_000 3_500 65_000 (JUST 5_000) EQUALS JUST 600
#ASSERT `s 9(1.2) — the employer's second additional contribution for the year in respect of an employee` 2024 (4%) 80_000 73_200 68_500 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 188
#ASSERT `s 9(1.2) — the employer's second additional contribution for the year in respect of an employee` 2024 (4%) 60_000 73_200 68_500 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 9(1.2) — the employer's second additional contribution for the year in respect of an employee` 2023 (4%) 80_000 73_200 68_500 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9(1.2) — the employer's second additional contribution for the year in respect of an employee` 2025 (4%) 80_000 73_200 68_500 (JUST 4_700) EQUALS JUST 0

-- The two sides of the same relation agree: an employee earning 80,000 in 2024 and the employer of that employee
-- each make the same three contributions (the rates are equal at (4.95%), (1%) and (4%) in these figures).
#ASSERT `s 8(1) — the employee's base contribution for the year` (4.95%) 80_000 3_500 65_000 NOTHING EQUALS `s 9(1) — the employer's base contribution for the year in respect of an employee` (4.95%) 80_000 3_500 65_000 NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 8(2) to (11): the excess amount, the overpayment and the prorating`

-- Employments (the fixtures are used by the cases below)
`CPP 80,000` MEANS `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` WITH
    `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS 80_000
    `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS TRUE
    `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS FALSE
`CPP 50,000` MEANS `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` WITH
    `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS 50_000
    `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS TRUE
    `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS FALSE
`CPP 100,000` MEANS `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` WITH
    `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS 100_000
    `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS TRUE
    `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS FALSE
`CPP 30,000` MEANS `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` WITH
    `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS 30_000
    `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS TRUE
    `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS FALSE
`CPP 40,000` MEANS `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` WITH
    `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS 40_000
    `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS TRUE
    `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS FALSE
`provincial 30,000` MEANS `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` WITH
    `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS 30_000
    `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS FALSE
    `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS TRUE
`provincial 60,000` MEANS `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` WITH
    `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS 60_000
    `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS FALSE
    `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS TRUE
`provincial 73,200` MEANS `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` WITH
    `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS 73_200
    `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS FALSE
    `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS TRUE
`provincial 66,600` MEANS `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` WITH
    `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS 66_600
    `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS FALSE
    `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS TRUE
`no wages` MEANS `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` WITH
    `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS 0
    `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS TRUE
    `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS FALSE

-- Case 1: one employer under this Act, wages 80,000 in 2024. Due: 3,217.50 + 650 + 188 = 4,055.50 (see the tests of 8(1) to (1.2)).
`facts 1: deductions equal what is due` MEANS `cp1 Facts about the contributions of an employee for a year` WITH
    `the year at hand` IS 2024
    `employments of the employee in the year` IS LIST `CPP 80,000`
    `contributory self-employed earnings of the employee for the year, if the employee is an individual described in section 10 to whom the provisions relating to the making of contributions apply` IS NOTHING
    `the contribution rate for employees for the year under this Act` IS (4.95%)
    `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year under this Act` IS (1%)
    `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year under this Act` IS (4%)
    `the base contribution rate for employees for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS (5.4%)
    `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS (1%)
    `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS (4%)
    `the employee's basic exemption for the year` IS 3_500
    `the employee's basic exemption for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 19(b) and (c)` IS 3_500
    `the employee's maximum contributory earnings for the year` IS 65_000
    `the employee's maximum contributory earnings for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 17(b) and (c) and 19(b) and (c)` IS 65_000
    `the employee's maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS 68_500
    `the employee's maximum pensionable earnings for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 17(b) and (c)` IS 68_500
    `the employee's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS 73_200
    `the employee's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 17.1(b) and (c)` IS 73_200
    `aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of the employee for the year on account of the employee's contributions under this Act` IS 4_055.5
    `aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of the employee for the year on account of the employee's contributions under this Act or under a provincial pension plan` IS 4_055.5
#ASSERT `s 8(4) — the ratio of the salary and wages under this Act to the aggregate, before 2024 limited by the maximum pensionable earnings and from 2024 by the additional maximum pensionable earnings` `facts 1: deductions equal what is due` EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `s 8(8) — the ratio of the salary and wages under this Act to the aggregate, each employment limited by the additional maximum pensionable earnings` `facts 1: deductions equal what is due` EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `s 8(2) — the excess amount calculated` `facts 1: deductions equal what is due` EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 8(2) — an excess amount has been paid` `facts 1: deductions equal what is due` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(3) — the overpayment made by the employee on account of the employee's contributions under this Act` `facts 1: deductions equal what is due` EQUALS JUST 0

